"# aos-gdb: stop an agent when a condition holds, look, go on\n\n`aos-gdb NAME` opens Python with `import aos.gdb as g` and `a = g.attach(NAME)` done (`--daemon D` or `$AOS_DAEMON`). A trigger is an ordinary hook on that agent (its own `<stack>/hooks.json`, name `gdb_...`, handler `lib/tools/agent/gdb_trigger`): when its condition holds it runs `aos-agent ctl pause --no-wait` and appends a note to `<stack>/gdb/log.jsonl`. The loop pauses between steps, so the step that saw the event finishes first.\n\n```python\na.stop_before_tool(\"write\")                 # that call still runs; block=True = that one call does not run\na.stop_on_tool_error(times=2)               # any tool exits non-zero or times out, twice in a row\na.stop_when(\"after_tool\", sh=\"grep -q secret\")                     # event JSON on stdin; exit 0 = hit, 10 = no hit\na.stop_when(\"before_tool\", py=lambda ev: ev[\"arguments\"].get(\"path\", \"\").endswith(\".env\"), once=True)\na.say(\"hi\"); a.wait_paused(); a.why(); a.where(); a.history(3); a.observed(3)\na.resume(); a.triggers(); a.remove(\"before_tool_1\"); a.clear()\n```\n\n- Every call prints the aos command behind it (`g.echo = False` stops that); a paused agent can also be resumed from a shell with `aos-agent ctl resume`.\n- Triggers are put in with `--on-error continue`: a broken condition or handler is one warning line, the agent does not stop or restart. `a.triggers()` shows `last_error`.\n- `why()` lists the notes since the last `a.resume()`, and says whether the agent is paused and whether the newest note belongs to this pause (another ctl command after it = the notes may be old).\n- Python conditions run in the hook process: they see `json`, `re`, `os` and builtins; pass other values as defaults (`lambda ev, x=x: ...`). They are refused at once when they use outer variables or unknown names.\n- Do not put triggers on another agent unless you were asked to debug it: it pauses that agent (aos/rules.json). More: `aos-gdb --help`, `help(a)` in the REPL, proto8/py/aos/apps/gdb/README.md.\n"
